@startuml access-readiness
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Selected access and container credential startup (FR-06)
caption Pre-claim readiness holds no secret. Every task container pulls the current selected credential when it starts.

state Entry <<choice>>
state "Read explicit access selection\nAPI or supported subscription; role models\nCredential reference only, never secret bytes" as Config
state "Check provider compatibility\nSelected mode, account, models, capabilities\nRequired evaluator and local budgets" as Precheck
state "Admission ready\nSelected mode/config recorded\nNo token fetched and no slot held" as AdmissionReady <<success>>

state "Start task container\nVerify run-bound identity and selected mode\nNew run or replacement for same run" as Start
state "Authenticate to credential manager\nRun-bound, read-only identity\nNo copied auth cache or embedded token" as StoreAuth
state "Fetch current access credential\nAPI credential or subscription access token\nRead version and issuer expiry when applicable" as Fetch
state Credential <<choice>>
state "Wait for current credential\nCentral auth owner refreshes/publishes if needed\nBounded wait; worker cannot refresh upstream" as WaitCredential
state "Initialize selected agent runtime\nUse fetched credential for supported mode\nVerify authentication and model access" as Initialize
state "Record credential readiness\nMode, version, expiry/recheck basis and evidence\nNever persist secret bytes" as Record
state "Container ready\nContinue this run at verified workflow boundary" as Ready <<success>>

state "Pause affected model work\nClassify in-flight outcome through operation guardrails\nNo blind replay of tools or model effects" as Recover
state "Needs attention\nCredential unavailable, expired, unsupported\nor selected account/usage blocked" as Attention <<attention>>

[*] --> Entry
Entry --> Config : [preclaim_check]
Entry --> Start : [worker_start or replacement_start]
Entry --> Recover : [auth_failure_during_run]
Config --> Precheck : selection and credential reference valid
Config --> Attention : missing/invalid selection or reference
Precheck --> AdmissionReady : selected mode and capabilities supported;\nknown limits/budgets permit
Precheck --> Attention : setup, entitlement, model, capability\nor usage readiness blocked
AdmissionReady --> [*] : return admission_ready

Start --> StoreAuth : current run identity verified
Start --> Attention : run identity or selected mode mismatch
Recover --> StoreAuth : prior operation reconciled;\nworkflow boundary verified
Recover --> Attention : in-flight effect or boundary unresolved
StoreAuth --> Fetch : manager read authorized for this run
StoreAuth --> Attention : manager unavailable or reader denied\nafter bounded recovery
Fetch --> Credential : selected credential and metadata returned
Fetch --> WaitCredential : absent, stale or read temporarily unavailable
Credential --> Initialize : [current for selected mode; expiry valid]
Credential --> WaitCredential : [expired, wrong mode or version stale]
WaitCredential --> Fetch : central owner published current version;\nretry within deadline
WaitCredential --> Attention : deadline or recovery budget exhausted
Initialize --> Record : selected runtime authenticates and model is usable
Initialize --> WaitCredential : authentication rejected due to stale token;\nnew version may be published
Initialize --> Attention : unsupported integration, entitlement\nor non-retryable authentication/usage failure
Record --> Ready : secret-free evidence persisted
Record --> Attention : readiness record unconfirmed
Ready --> [*] : return container_ready
Attention --> [*] : return attention

note right of Fetch
  The worker reads the CURRENT credential at EVERY container start,
  including a replacement container for an interrupted run.
  API mode may use a static API key; subscription mode needs a
  supported worker-usable access token. OpenBao is the preferred
  credential manager behind a replaceable adapter.
  A worker never reads the renewable login or auth.json.
end note
note bottom of Ready
  The selected mode never silently switches to billable API access.
  Startup must finish before agent work or Jira work-start update.
  Re-entry after a crash uses process-restart-recovery.puml:
  same run only at a verified checkpoint, with fresh role sessions.
end note
@enduml
